Once a \code{tbl_now} carries a confirmation process, "how many cases were there"
has three different answers, and which one you want depends on the question:
\itemize{
\item \strong{\code{get_latest_reported_cases()}} (the existing function) counts everything
that was ever \emph{reported}, whatever the laboratory later said. It is what a
nowcast of the reporting process predicts.
\item \strong{\code{get_latest_confirmed()}} counts only the cases that came back
\strong{confirmed}. Pending and retracted cases are not counted.
\item \strong{\code{get_net_confirmed()}} counts \strong{confirmed minus retracted}: the running
total as a surveillance system would publish it, which can go \strong{down} when
a case is withdrawn.
}

That last one is the quantity a \code{count-cumulative} stream actually reports,
and the one \pkg{diseasenowcasting}'s signed-increment (Skellam / SkNB)
